: "Under the Ptolemaic rulers of Egypt, every vessel that docked in Alexandria's harbor was searched by royal officials.", "s": 6.656, "e": 14.974}, {"text": "Any scrolls found on board were seized and taken to the library.", "s": 15.094, "e": 19.489}, {"text": "Scribes would copy the texts by hand, and then keep the priceless originals for the library while returning the cheap copies to the ship captains.", "s": 19.609, "e": 29.354}, {"text": "Thanks to this ruthless policy, Alexandria gathered nearly half a million scrolls from across the known world.", "s": 29.474, "e": 36.834}]}